      "text_snapshot": "Perfect. Now I have the full context. Let me provide the summary:\nProblem:\nEntire Brain's plugin lacked client-side hosted fact sync: repositories could not automatically publish local facts to and pull teammates' facts from a hosted brain service. Users had no way to connect a local repository to its hosted brain, sync facts across branches and machines, or receive server-stamped author attribution.\nSolution:\nThe branch adds end-to-end hosted fact sync with four foundational components:\nRepository connection — entire brain connect binds a repo to its hosted brain by storing repo ID, API base URL, and jurisdiction (non-secrets; tokens mint fresh per call). It resolves placement from entire repo whereami --json or accepts explicit flags, validates URLs, strips /api/v1 suffix (factsync appends it), and performs an initial pull on first connect.\nAuthor field — Facts now carry an optional Author field for display attribution, stamped server-side during pull and excluded from content ID (two facts differing only in Author are deduplicated). Client egress clears Author before upload so server-verified attribution survives; local re-distill or legacy servers without authors don't erase existing handles.\nAutomatic sync in daemon — The watch tick runs hostedFactsSyncAndPull every 15 minutes (cursor-throttled) on idle ticks too, publishing local facts and pulling teammates' facts. Session-end hook syncs current and default branches on every exit path, ensuring facts flow immediately. hostedFactsSyncAndPull is never-fails: every gated/soft failure logs to stderr, local brain remains unchanged.\nBlind-spot note — Empty query results on connected-but-unsynced branches now surface an actionable note: \"this repository is connected to a hosted brain but branch X has never synced; run entire brain facts sync\" — more useful than the generic multi-branch hint.\nThe sync loop reads local facts, publishes via CAS (compare-and-swap), records per-branch sync state, fetches the settled head with server-stamped authors, and merges into the local store; teammates' facts become first-class in brief/recall without manual commands beyond initial connect.",
